      "caption": "For I/you/we/they, the verb never changes. The helper <b>do</b> handles the negative and the question."
    },
    {
      "type": "steps",
      "title": "How to make a negative",
      "steps": [
        {
          "label": "Start with the person",
          "ex": "They"
        },
        {
          "label": "Add don't",
          "ex": "They <b>don't</b>"
        },
        {
          "label": "Add the base verb — no -s",
          "ex": "They don't <b>like</b> maths"
        }
      ],
      "caption": "Don't already carries the negative meaning, so the verb after it stays in its simplest form."
    },
