  "can_do": [
    "I can talk about my everyday routine with I, you, we and they.",
    "I can say what I like, love and hate, and make negatives with don't.",
    "I can ask <i>Do you…?</i> and answer <i>Yes, I do</i> / <i>No, we don't</i>."
  ],
  "summary": [
    "For I/you/we/they, the verb stays in its base form: <i>I play, you play, we play, they play</i>.",
    "Negative: <b>don't</b> + base verb — <i>I don't like maths</i>.",
    "Question: <b>Do</b> + person + base verb — <i>Do you play tennis?</i>",
    "Short answers: <i>Yes, I do. / No, they don't.</i> — never repeat the main verb.",
    "Use like/love/hate + a noun or + -ing: <i>I love pizza, I love swimming</i>."
  ]
}
